  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Crataegus mexicana",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crataegus_mexicana",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1352542402,
      "text": "Crataegus mexicana is a species of hawthorn known by the common names tejocote, manzanita, tejocotera and Mexican hawthorn. It is native to the mountains of Mexico and parts of Guatemala, and has been introduced in the Andes. The fruit of this species is one of the most useful among hawthorns."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Crataegus mexicana",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crataegus_mexicana",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 171808506,
      "text": "Crataegus mexicana, conocida comúnmente como manzanita, manzanilla, manzana de Indias, manzana chilena, tejocotera y tejocote, es un arbusto o árbol frutal pequeño nativo de Mesoamérica hoy, El Salvador, México y Guatemala, donde se conoce comúnmente como manzanilla."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Aubépine du Mexique",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aub%C3%A9pine_du_Mexique",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 231327189,
      "text": "L'aubépine du Mexique, aussi appelée Tejocote, du náhuatl \"texocotl\" qui signifie \"pierre acide\", est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Rosaceae. C'est une aubépine originaire de l'État de Chiapas au Mexique et du Guatemala, Honduras, Costa Rica en Amérique centrale."
    }
  },
